# Quality Gate Propagation Risk
# SSOT: unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/quality-gates-library-template.sh
#       unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/quality-gates-service-template.sh
# Rollout: unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-unified.py
# Trigger: bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/repo-management/run-all-setup.sh --rollout-first

RULE: When editing `scripts/quality-gates.sh` in ANY downstream repo (service, library, api, ui),
      changes WILL be overwritten on the next `run-all-setup.sh --rollout-first` run.
      ALWAYS propagate fixes to the codex template SSOT first.

WHY: `rollout-quality-gates-unified.py` reads the codex templates and overwrites every repo's
     `scripts/quality-gates.sh`. A local-only fix survives until the next rollout, then vanishes.

DO:
  1. Edit the codex template FIRST:
     - Libraries: `unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/quality-gates-library-template.sh`
     - Services:  `unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/quality-gates-service-template.sh`
  2. Optionally apply the same change to the downstream repo for immediate effect.
  3. Run `python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-unified.py --dry-run`
     to preview what repos would be updated.
  4. Document repo-specific deviations in the repo's `QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md`.

NEVER:
  - Edit only the downstream `scripts/quality-gates.sh` without updating the codex template.
  - Use `rollout-quality-gates-unified.py` to REVERT intentional downstream deviations;
    deviations belong in QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md, not in the template.

DEVIATIONS ALLOWED:
  - Per-repo PACKAGE_NAME, SOURCE_DIR, LOCAL_DEPS settings (these are repo-specific placeholders).
  - Entries in QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md for documented exceptions.
  - The rollout script preserves these placeholders and the bypass audit file.

CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md
